{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::domain::NodeContents::format` presents the retained\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_contents` as text for an agent:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Present these retained contents as text for an agent.\n    /// Use the same observation described by fingerprint().\n    /// Everything needed for presentation is retained in this value.\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nFormatting uses the retained value and completes without further resource reads\nor fallible preparation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\n\n**Obligations drawn from the text**\n1. `format` presents the retained node contents as agent text.\n2. It uses the same observation that `fingerprint()` describes.\n3. It needs nothing beyond the retained value. It does no further resource reads and no fallible preparation.\n\n**Coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads a snapshot while the node content is \"before\".\n  - It asserts `snapshot.content.format()` equals \"before\".\n  - It then changes the underlying graph content to \"after\".\n  - Afterwards it asserts `fingerprint()` still equals `snapshot.fingerprint`, and `format()` still returns \"before\".\n  - Together these show that `format` uses the retained observation, the same one the fingerprint describes, and does not re-read the resource.\n  - It also asserts that the graph's recorded reads remain `[1]`, so `format` triggers no further read.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` covers the real `HabeasNodeContent` type.\n  - It prepares the content from an already-resolved input that points at a nonexistent file, `missing.rs`.\n  - It asserts that `format()` still contains the supplied text and the path.\n  - This shows `format` does no filesystem resolution and cannot fail on a missing file.\n\n**Other implementation**\n`src/authoring/sdk.rs#impl[ReviewContent/NodeContents]/fn[format]` is a plain `self.text.clone()` with no conditional or transformation. That is a pass-through, so the testing exemption applies and it needs no separate test.\n\nI found no gaps.",
  "references": "4b0865bf1df20bde0e64bbee5c587e1038736063c4b918bbd059337ce7c01c1a",
